Source: reform-qcacld2
Priority: optional
Maintainer: robot <reform@reform.repo>
Section: non-free/kernel
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 14), dh-sequence-single-binary
Standards-Version: 4.7.0

# this is arch:any because of #1134628
Package: reform-qcacld2
Architecture: any
Description: Remaining parts of the out-of-tree driver for QCA9733 wifi
 The QCA9733 is contained in i.MX8MP module for MNT Reform/Pocket Reform.
 .
 Since kernel version 7.3, ath10k_sdio works with qca9377 wifi in the Pocket
 Reform, making the qcacld2 dkms driver obsolete.
 .
 This package exists to ensure that /etc/modprobe.d/reform-qcacld2.conf and
 /etc/kernel/postinst.d/zz-reform-qcacld2 are getting removed. The former used
 to blacklist ath10k_sdio but that is already done by
 /usr/lib/modprobe.d/reform.conf shipped by reform-tools. The latter used force
 an installation of the latest reform-qcacld2 package on every kernel
 installation via a kernel postinstallation hook.
 .
 This package also ships the required firmware blobs to make sure that qcacld2
 for kernel versions before 7.3 can still function correctly.
